#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-home — canonical resolver CLI for the ~/.claude path resolver.

Spec backlink: coordinator/docs/wiki/machine-local-registry.md §4a

Naked-Python entrypoint: it IS the implementation's CLI trampoline. The
former bash veneer resolved a python3/python interpreter and execed
_claude_home.py; a python3-shebang script needs neither step — Python is
already running. This file locates its co-located _claude_home.py (fail-loud
if absent, matching the bash predecessor's guard) and dispatches straight
into its _main().

Kept extensionless (not renamed to claude-home.py) — callers on PATH
(shutil.which("claude-home"), bare claude-home <subcommand> shell-outs)
depend on the exact bareword name.

No sh/python polyglot trampoline line (removed 2026-07-28; this docstring
was briefly demoted to a #-comment header in the same change and is
restored here as a real docstring, since a module docstring is required at
this structural boundary — CLAUDE.md § Implementation Standards — and
carries no command-substitution span, which is the actual property that
matters, not the mere presence of a docstring). The retired trampoline
shape cost ~326ms/invocation on Windows versus a direct python3 invocation
(1306ms via the shim vs 980ms direct, byte-identical output — measured by
coordinator/bin/check-sh-suffix-polyglot.py's docstring, source-of-record
state/audits/2026-07-20-sh-suffixed-python-trampolines.md in the
DoE-claude clone, not this repo — the path is qualified deliberately, and
its absence here is not evidence it is missing), paid unconditionally on
every call,
independent of the separate command-substitution hazard
coordinator/bin/tests/test_no_bin_docstring_command_substitution.py gates
(a backtick-delimited or dollar-paren command-substitution span inside a
docstring is live shell text to a mistaken bash <file> invocation and can
hang forever on a span that resolves to a stdin-blocking command).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
_IMPL = _SCRIPT_DIR / "_claude_home.py"

if not _IMPL.is_file():
    sys.stderr.write(f"claude-home: implementation not found at {_IMPL}\n")
    sys.exit(1)

if str(_SCRIPT_DIR) not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, str(_SCRIPT_DIR))

from _claude_home import _main  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(_main(sys.argv))
